{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":47056,"duration_api_ms":47027,"num_turns":10,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"ce10b7d0-81cf-47dd-b63b-814e4febf8fa","total_cost_usd":0.29422299999999996,"usage":{"input_tokens":5,"cache_creation_input_tokens":28040,"cache_read_input_tokens":115696,"output_tokens":2444,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":28040,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":5,"outputTokens":2444,"cacheReadInputTokens":115696,"cacheCreationInputTokens":28040,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.29422299999999996,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Two amendments describe mass-basis bugs that have already been fixed in the current code (routing-basis variables are used throughout shrimp_feeding and its tests). The third amendment identifies a real backward-compatibility regression: the v3→v4 migration is a no-op, leaving reserve_g at 0.0 for legacy saves, but reserve is now the mandatory funding source for hatching and juvenile maturation — causing valid legacy colonies to stall immediately after upgrade.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-5-c3828380","decision":"reject","rationale":"The current code at shrimp.rs:142-153 already converts food demand and periphyton consumption to the routing/organic-matter basis before computing detritus demand: `food_demand_route_g = algae_detrital_mass_g(food_demand_biomass_g, n_to_c_ratio)`, `periph_consumed_route_g = algae_detrital_mass_g(periph_consumed_biomass_g, n_to_c_ratio)`, and `detritus_demand_route_g = (food_demand_route_g - periph_consumed_route_g).max(0.0)`. The variable names include `_route_g` suffixes throughout. The claimed periphyton-biomass-vs-detritus mismatch does not exist in the current implementation."},{"amendment_id":"fr-5-d1fd0cd7","decision":"reject","rationale":"The test at shrimp.rs:833-877 already works on the routing/organic-matter basis. It computes `periphyton_consumed_route_g` via `algae_detrital_mass_g(periphyton_consumed_biomass_g, n_to_c_ratio)` (line 862-863), `detritus_consumed_route_g` from the detritus pool delta (line 864, already in organic-matter grams), and `max_daily_intake_route_g` via `algae_detrital_mass_g(...)` (line 851). The assertion at line 868 sums `periphyton_consumed_route_g + detritus_consumed_route_g` — both in the same mass basis. No incompatible units are being summed."},{"amendment_id":"fr-5-847e2a07","decision":"accept","rationale":"The v3→v4 migration (save.rs:329-331) is a no-op, so legacy saves deserialize with `animal.reserve_g = 0.0` via `#[serde(default)]`. However, `fund_live_shrimp_biomass` (shrimp.rs:645-656) now gates both hatching (via `fund_hatched_clutch_biomass`, called at line 471) and juvenile maturation (line 558) on having sufficient reserve. A valid v3 colony with near-hatch egg cohorts or ready-to-mature juveniles will therefore fail all those transitions immediately after loading, causing the simulation to diverge from the pre-upgrade trajectory. The migration should seed reserve_g proportionally to the existing colony size. The test at save_load.rs:274-320 codifies the zero-reserve outcome, so this regression would persist unnoticed."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"88323864-13e1-4a10-b61e-219d8e594075"}
